WEBVTT

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.681
[girl] <i>Hyakkao Private Academy.</i>

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.350
<i>Known for its prestige and traditions,</i>

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:21.354
<i>this school is about to celebrate</i>
<i>it's 121st anniversary.</i>

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:25.358
<i>A hierarchy exists</i>
<i>within the ranks of its elite students.</i>

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.111
<i>It's not your grades</i>
<i>or how you do in sports</i>

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.487
<i>that will get you noticed here.</i>

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.532
<i>That would be…</i>

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.619
<i>gambling!</i>

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.413
<i>Gambling is everything!</i>

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:41.750
<i>And if you're good at it, then you can get</i>
<i>away with pretty much anything you want.</i>

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:45.336
Oh yeah. And cheating is okay
if you don't get caught.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.130
This part is really important!

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.674
<i>Let's say you lose it all</i>
<i>and end up owing the house?</i>

00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:50.633
<i>What then?</i>

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:56.765
<i>A donation totaling the amount of the debt</i>
<i>to the student council is required.</i>

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:58.850
<i>Otherwise, your ranking will fall.</i>

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:02.020
<i>Anyone that falls</i>
<i>to the bottom of the ranking list</i>

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:03.897
<i>will be treated as a pet.</i>

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.774
<i>Boys are called "Fido,"</i>

00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:07.776
<i>and girls are called "Mittens."</i>

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:11.029
<i>They have to deal with bullying</i>
<i>from other students just about every day</i>

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:14.282
House pets aren't allowed
to disobey human orders.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.829
<i>And this is me, Tsuzura Hanatemari.</i>

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.040
<i>And yeah. I got water dumped on me.</i>

00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:23.333
<i>I'm a Mitten.</i>

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.169
<i>The one the pouring water is Kokoro Aiura.</i>

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.213
<i>She's the top gambler in our class.</i>

00:01:28.296 --> 00:01:31.216
Nice to meet you. Fresh blood for me.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:34.552
<i>Oh right. You're probably</i>
<i>wondering who she was talking to.</i>

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:36.513
<i>This is Mary Saotome.</i>

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.266
<i>She's a new transfer student here,</i>
<i>but we went to grade school together.</i>

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:44.354
<i>The two of us meeting again</i>
<i>after this long must be fate!</i>

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.233
You have to be careful, Mary.

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:51.486
I've heard they tend
to target the new transfer students.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.489
SPEED PRESIDENT CARD GAME

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:57.450
<i>Mary didn't waste any time</i>
<i>and gambled right away,</i>

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.702
<i>but was a total amateur</i>
<i>who stood no chance</i>

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.122
<i>against Aiura's cheating ways, and bam!</i>

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:05.208
<i>Mary was 200,000 yen in debt!</i>

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.169
<i>But thanks to some cash I had hidden away,</i>

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:10.755
<i>I was able</i>
<i>to give her the money to try again.</i>

00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:13.758
REMATCH

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:20.515
<i>Unfortunately,</i>
<i>she cheated again. Dun-dun-dun.</i>

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:22.600
<i>But Mary was able to figure it out!</i>

00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:24.102
<i>Ta-da!</i>

00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:28.439
[Tsuzura] <i>Mary pulled it off</i>
<i>and won it all back.</i>

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.652
<i>She made 200,000 yen on the day</i>
<i>she transferred into the school,</i>

00:02:32.735 --> 00:02:34.737
<i>and made it to the top of our class.</i>

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.990
<i>That's as far as we've gotten with Mary,</i>

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:39.492
<i>and where the rest of our story's</i>
<i>about to begin.</i>

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.619
<i>But I'll tell you a secret.</i>

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.872
<i>That made me realize</i>
<i>Mary isn't just a girl</i>

00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:46.332
<i>who got enrolled thanks</i>
<i>to her rich family.</i>

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:49.627
<i>It's like I can see her hand</i>
<i>reaching out to me.</i>

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:55.133
<i>I want her to be my prince!</i>

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.264
A WEEK LATER

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:04.517
[footsteps approaching]

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.645
<i>I'm not making any friends.</i>

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.064
[Mary] <i>Why not?</i>

00:03:10.148 --> 00:03:12.775
<i>Everyone was watching me</i>
<i>when I played against Aiura.</i>

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.571
<i>I've made sure to study and have answered</i>
<i>everything in class perfectly</i>

00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:18.281
<i>so no one could make fun of me.</i>

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.284
<i>My make-up is natural</i>
<i>and freaking awesome.</i>

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.786
<i>My nails are a conservative pastel-pink,</i>

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.539
<i>and I've been making sure</i>
<i>to be extra nice.</i>

00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:28.541
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:31.711
<i>I don't have much hope</i>
<i>for my life plan at this point.</i>

00:03:33.087 --> 00:03:34.297
<i>When people are born,</i>

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.674
<i>they naturally tend</i>
<i>to fall into hierarchies.</i>

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:40.178
<i>Endurance, intelligence, </i>

00:03:40.261 --> 00:03:44.682
<i>appearance, sensibility,</i>
<i>and don't forget money.</i>

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:48.603
<i>I hate how society divides its people up</i>
<i>into winners and losers</i>

00:03:48.686 --> 00:03:50.939
<i>based on circumstances we can't control.</i>

00:03:51.022 --> 00:03:55.109
<i>That's why I decided to transfer</i>
<i>to this school as an honor student.</i>

00:03:55.693 --> 00:03:58.655
<i>By the time I leave this school,</i>
<i>I'll be a winner</i>

00:03:59.614 --> 00:04:02.158
Although,
at this rate I'm not so sure anymore.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.826
Hey, Mary?

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.411
-Uh, um…
-Huh?

00:04:05.495 --> 00:04:07.455
Oh. Hi, Mary.

00:04:07.538 --> 00:04:09.916
How has school been?
Are you getting used to it?

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.293
Yeah, I guess.

00:04:12.377 --> 00:04:14.504
Did you need something, Hanatemari?

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.172
Oh. Well, I was hoping,

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.841
and I know
that this is kinda out of the blue,

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:22.303
but would you like to…
would you want to…

00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:24.180
Could we please be friends?

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.308
Hmm.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.143
Sure. I guess.

00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.895
I guess that was presumptuous.

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:33.064
I'm sure you already have
a bunch of friends.

00:04:33.147 --> 00:04:35.858
And you might not like me anyway.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:36.859
I'm slow.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.696
I'll probably just end up
being a house pet forever.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.572
Never mind. It's fine.

00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:44.575
-Forget I even asked.
-What's that pathetic look on your face?

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:48.329
[Mary] You did this
when I was up against Aiura too.

00:04:49.914 --> 00:04:51.291
Why do you have this?

00:04:51.374 --> 00:04:53.501
Aren't you supposed to be a house pet?

00:04:53.584 --> 00:04:56.504
If you have this kinda money,
why don't you use it for yourself?

00:04:56.587 --> 00:04:58.631
Even if I could get out
of being a house pet,

00:04:58.715 --> 00:05:00.008
it wouldn't be for long.

00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:02.760
And I wouldn't know
what to do with myself if I did.

00:05:03.886 --> 00:05:05.430
Why are you always like this?

00:05:05.513 --> 00:05:07.807
No! I'm sorry!

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:08.725
I'm sorry.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:15.440
Hanatemari,
would you mind explaining something to me?

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.191
Huh?

00:05:19.068 --> 00:05:22.238
[Tsuzura] Well, I think it's just because
that wasn't a whole lot of money.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.156
Really?

00:05:23.239 --> 00:05:26.326
To the kids at this school,
200,000 yen is allowance money.

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:28.244
Something to buy school supplies with.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:31.664
I don't think it would be, really, enough
to prove that you're a good gambler.

00:05:31.748 --> 00:05:34.834
You'd probably have to play
with higher stakes than that.

00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:38.129
Wow. I guess this school
really is that ridiculous.

00:05:38.212 --> 00:05:40.882
Oh. I forgot to ask earlier.
What are you drinking?

00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:42.633
Huh? Let me show you.

00:05:43.426 --> 00:05:44.761
I have one of these.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.763
Oh! That is so cute!

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:49.515
I've been carrying this thing around
since middle school.

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:52.143
I can't remember the last time
I saw a water bottle.

00:05:52.226 --> 00:05:53.436
Uh…

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.646
<i>Is that why</i>
<i>they've been looking down on me?</i>

00:05:56.731 --> 00:06:00.777
So after school, there are gambling dens
that pop up, right?

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.528
Would you mind showing me around?

00:06:02.612 --> 00:06:04.947
Yes, of course!

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.532
Which one of them did you wanna visit?

00:06:07.158 --> 00:06:08.785
Well, I was thinking,

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:12.288
why don't we pop in
to whichever one is the least popular?

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.751
Are you sure this is gonna be okay?

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:17.794
This will be fine.

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:20.088
If this spot isn't totally dead,

00:06:20.171 --> 00:06:22.673
it'll be that much easier
for me to take it over.

00:06:22.757 --> 00:06:23.716
Huh?

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.302
I think I figured out the secret
to being a winner.

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.554
And it's to be the financier of a den.

00:06:28.638 --> 00:06:29.931
Just watch.

00:06:30.014 --> 00:06:33.184
Fastest way to the top.
This is gonna be a blast.

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:18.104
TWIN

00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:22.984
[Mary] Excuse me.

00:07:24.902 --> 00:07:26.737
[Mary] Anyone here?
-Huh?

00:07:26.821 --> 00:07:29.240
Oh, hi! Welcome! So sorry.

00:07:29.323 --> 00:07:30.908
I didn't notice you come in
at all--

00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:32.368
Whoa!

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:33.995
Are you all right?

00:07:34.996 --> 00:07:36.706
Welcome to the literary club!

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.001
I'm the president, Yukimi Togakushi!

00:07:40.084 --> 00:07:42.253
Were you two thinking
about becoming members today?

00:07:42.336 --> 00:07:43.463
No. We're good.

00:07:43.546 --> 00:07:45.131
Yeah. Thought so.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.553
It's embarrassing to admit,
but it's always pretty dead in here.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:51.888
We don't really get patrons.

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:54.515
I'm the only club member
that hasn't ghosted yet.

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:57.852
<i>Perfect.</i>
<i>Now, to figure out how to pull it off.</i>

00:07:57.935 --> 00:07:59.770
Oh. How lucky for me.

00:08:00.271 --> 00:08:02.023
There are visitors.

00:08:02.106 --> 00:08:04.734
Oh! Yeah, sorry. We're a little busy.

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:06.027
Send them out.

00:08:07.612 --> 00:08:09.030
Huh?

00:08:18.122 --> 00:08:19.790
MITTENS

00:08:20.374 --> 00:08:21.834
-Mikura.
-Right.

00:08:22.752 --> 00:08:26.380
As of this present reading,
the club's access to this room is revoked.

00:08:26.464 --> 00:08:28.341
You can no longer this space.

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:30.968
So, please vacate immediately.

00:08:31.594 --> 00:08:33.846
Huh?
I can't just do that right away. There's--

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:37.016
When did you last pay usage fees
for this room?

00:08:37.099 --> 00:08:38.976
Surely you got our collection letters.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.102
Uh…

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:43.105
Who is she?
I don't like how she came in here.

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:44.106
Right. You're new.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.109
She's the Chair of the Student Council
Public Morals Committee.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:48.486
Sachiko Juraku.

00:08:48.569 --> 00:08:51.614
The gambling dens here
are under her jurisdiction.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:54.784
Hm.

00:08:55.451 --> 00:08:57.245
What's the matter, Yukimi?

00:08:59.121 --> 00:09:01.332
[Mary] What do you think
about letting me use this place?

00:09:01.415 --> 00:09:02.250
Huh?

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:05.878
You?

00:09:06.462 --> 00:09:08.798
Let me take over running this den for you.

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:12.635
I'll improve the revenue stream,
and I'll even pay a higher usage fee.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.220
Interesting.

00:09:14.303 --> 00:09:16.264
And who are you?

00:09:16.347 --> 00:09:19.600
First year, Hana class. Mary Saotome.

00:09:19.684 --> 00:09:21.394
Can we slow down for a second?

00:09:21.477 --> 00:09:24.188
I can pay you back next month.
Even what's overdue.

00:09:24.272 --> 00:09:26.649
I think it would be better
to go with someone brand new

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:30.069
instead of placing the same losing bet
on a person that has failed you.

00:09:30.152 --> 00:09:30.987
Hmm?

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.739
How fascinating. Let's do this, then.

00:09:34.323 --> 00:09:37.994
Mary, Yukimi, you will gamble.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.746
-The winner will control this den.
-Hmm.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.873
But, I…

00:09:42.957 --> 00:09:44.125
<i>Excellent.</i>

00:09:44.208 --> 00:09:45.126
<i>I was optimistic,</i>

00:09:45.209 --> 00:09:49.005
<i>but there was no way I could've imagined</i>
<i>things falling into place like this.</i>

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:52.133
All right. The minimum buy-in
will be one million yen.

00:09:53.676 --> 00:09:56.053
It's the same amount
as a gambling den's setup fee.

00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:58.681
I wouldn't worry. The loser pays.

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:00.891
So you'll owe me nothing if you win.

00:10:00.975 --> 00:10:02.685
<i>That's so much money.</i>

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.979
I guess I'll do it.
It's not like I have a choice.

00:10:05.062 --> 00:10:05.896
<i>Oh crap!</i>

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:08.232
What's the matter, Mary?

00:10:08.316 --> 00:10:09.650
How much can you put down?

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.030
I only have 200,000.

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:16.949
Fine. I will front the money for the bet.

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:19.535
If you lose, then I'll expect my 800,000.

00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:22.913
Don't do it, Mary! You don't want
to owe the Student Council money.

00:10:22.997 --> 00:10:24.999
But you do want the den, right?

00:10:25.082 --> 00:10:27.168
You should be willing to accept the risk.

00:10:29.378 --> 00:10:32.673
Hanatemari,
I have to prove myself somewhere.

00:10:36.344 --> 00:10:38.179
Fine then. I'll help.

00:10:38.262 --> 00:10:41.807
-Huh?
-I'll front 500,000. I want to.

00:10:41.891 --> 00:10:43.059
You do?

00:10:43.726 --> 00:10:44.644
Hmm.

00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:51.359
Very well. Mikura, start us off.

00:10:51.442 --> 00:10:52.443
Yes.

00:10:53.819 --> 00:10:55.946
[suspenseful music playing]

00:10:56.822 --> 00:11:00.326
The game we'll be playing today
is known as "Three Hit Dice."

00:11:00.409 --> 00:11:02.286
As the dealer, I will toss the dice.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.497
It's a simple concept to understand.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.333
The goal is to guess
what numbers on the dice will be rolled.

00:11:07.917 --> 00:11:09.710
The dice shall read as follows.

00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:12.213
One, two, and three will be "down."

00:11:12.296 --> 00:11:15.716
Four, five, and six
will be designated as "up."

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.093
As for you two,

00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:20.346
I'll have each of you guess the result
of each roll before they occur.

00:11:20.429 --> 00:11:24.475
Whichever of you to correctly call
a sequence combination will be the winner.

00:11:24.558 --> 00:11:27.770
For example,
let's say our match is A vs B.

00:11:27.853 --> 00:11:29.730
A guesses "U-D-D,"

00:11:29.814 --> 00:11:32.358
and B guesses "D-U-D"

00:11:32.441 --> 00:11:34.318
Then the dealer will throw the dice.

00:11:34.819 --> 00:11:38.489
A's guess of "U-D-D" appears first
in this scenario.

00:11:38.572 --> 00:11:40.616
Which means A would be the winner.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.451
Please write down your guesses.

00:11:42.952 --> 00:11:45.746
Then pass your cards to me,
and I will roll.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.707
Sorry about this,

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.959
but I need
to keep protecting this gambling den.

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:51.919
I'm going to win this.

00:11:52.002 --> 00:11:54.171
<i>If I win, the gambling den is mine.</i>

00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:56.257
<i>If I lose, I owe a lot of money.</i>

00:11:57.216 --> 00:11:59.427
<i>It'll be hard</i>
<i>to get out of debt once I have it,</i>

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:01.762
<i>and I'll probably end up becoming</i>
<i>a house pet.</i>

00:12:02.346 --> 00:12:04.765
<i>I don't have a choice. I have to win.</i>

00:12:04.849 --> 00:12:06.100
<i>I will win!</i>

00:12:11.814 --> 00:12:13.899
The cards are in,
and the game will begin now.

00:12:15.609 --> 00:12:17.069
Here's the first toss.

00:12:19.029 --> 00:12:20.281
First toss is down.

00:12:22.783 --> 00:12:25.244
<i>If she wrote down</i>
<i>the same guess as Togakushi,</i>

00:12:25.327 --> 00:12:27.037
<i>then the match would be a draw right now.</i>

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:29.790
Second toss, down.

00:12:29.874 --> 00:12:31.876
<i>But other than that, well…</i>

00:12:32.376 --> 00:12:35.963
<i>The likelihood of the die throw landing</i>
<i>in a up or down position</i>

00:12:36.046 --> 00:12:38.299
<i>is the same at one in two chances.</i>

00:12:38.382 --> 00:12:42.511
<i>With these three consecutive tosses,</i>
<i>the probability would be cubed.</i>

00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:45.055
<i>That would put it</i>
<i>at a one-in-eight chance.</i>

00:12:45.139 --> 00:12:46.056
Third toss now.

00:12:48.184 --> 00:12:49.059
Up.

00:12:49.143 --> 00:12:50.186
<i>And there we go.</i>

00:12:50.269 --> 00:12:52.938
<i>Whatever you end up writing,</i>
<i>your odds of winning are the same.</i>

00:12:53.022 --> 00:12:55.775
<i>Sure,</i>
<i>if you fall into the typical traps.</i>

00:12:55.858 --> 00:12:58.068
<i>It's a big mistake to think that way.</i>

00:12:58.152 --> 00:13:01.697
<i>If we were just tossing the dice</i>
<i>and guessing individual results,</i>

00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:04.575
<i>then the probability</i>
<i>for any combination is the same.</i>

00:13:05.201 --> 00:13:09.205
<i>But guessing which combination is going</i>
<i>to come up first is totally different.</i>

00:13:09.914 --> 00:13:11.832
<i>There are always going to be combinations</i>

00:13:11.916 --> 00:13:14.126
<i>that end up being more probable</i>
<i>than others.</i>

00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:17.713
<i>This is what's commonly known</i>
<i>as a gambler's fallacy.</i>

00:13:18.297 --> 00:13:22.718
<i>U-U-D, U-D-D, D-D-U, D-U-U.</i>

00:13:23.219 --> 00:13:25.429
<i>That's all possible combinations</i>
<i>of letters</i>

00:13:25.513 --> 00:13:28.849
<i>where the result appears twice in a row</i>
<i>after just eight tosses.</i>

00:13:28.933 --> 00:13:32.561
<i>So for us to have a result,</i>
<i>with three down or up rolls in a row,</i>

00:13:32.645 --> 00:13:36.482
<i>we'd have to expect that</i>
<i>as the estimated value of 14 tosses.</i>

00:13:36.565 --> 00:13:38.442
<i>The thrill at the core of dice games</i>

00:13:38.526 --> 00:13:41.111
<i>stems from the slight fluctuations</i>
<i>in probability.</i>

00:13:41.195 --> 00:13:43.781
<i>A small difference</i>
<i>can lead to big results.</i>

00:13:44.365 --> 00:13:46.033
Fifth toss is down.

00:13:46.116 --> 00:13:49.787
<i>With all that being said,</i>
<i>my guess was "U-U-D."</i>

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:51.789
<i>It's the most probable pattern.</i>

00:13:52.665 --> 00:13:54.875
<i>I'd be surprised</i>
<i>if she didn't know that too.</i>

00:13:54.959 --> 00:13:56.168
<i>So, I can't get cocky.</i>

00:13:57.086 --> 00:13:59.171
Sixth toss. Up.

00:13:59.255 --> 00:14:01.382
<i>This is really</i>
<i>just a countermeasure</i>

00:14:01.465 --> 00:14:03.133
<i>so I won't be at a disadvantage.</i>

00:14:03.717 --> 00:14:05.386
<i>I've done everything I can.</i>

00:14:05.469 --> 00:14:08.722
<i>Whatever may happen after this</i>
<i>is for fate to decide.</i>

00:14:08.806 --> 00:14:09.890
The seventh toss.

00:14:10.808 --> 00:14:11.642
Up.

00:14:12.977 --> 00:14:14.395
This means the game is over.

00:14:14.478 --> 00:14:15.396
-Uh…
-Huh?

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.648
D-U-U was rolled.

00:14:17.731 --> 00:14:20.150
Miss Togakushi is the winner.

00:14:20.234 --> 00:14:22.653
No way! How could Mary have lost?

00:14:22.736 --> 00:14:26.031
Then, as we agreed,
Yukimi will retain den rights.

00:14:26.115 --> 00:14:29.785
And I believe
I'm owed a million yen from Mary.

00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:33.455
You don't look too happy.

00:14:33.539 --> 00:14:36.125
I thought you'd be
a more gracious winner, Yukimi.

00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:37.543
Oh. I, uh…

00:14:38.127 --> 00:14:39.670
Right. I won.

00:14:39.753 --> 00:14:42.298
So, that means I can keep using this space
for the club, right?

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:43.757
Of course, it does.

00:14:43.841 --> 00:14:46.677
Do you have any objections to that?

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.262
N-no! I'm so relieved.

00:14:48.345 --> 00:14:49.179
Mary…

00:14:51.432 --> 00:14:53.684
One more round. Let's play one more round.

00:14:53.767 --> 00:14:55.436
Hmm.

00:14:56.937 --> 00:14:58.898
[Mary] I don't care
if the buy-in is twice as much!

00:14:58.981 --> 00:15:00.900
I promise I'll pay it back if I lose!

00:15:00.983 --> 00:15:03.068
What? Hold on just a minute!

00:15:03.152 --> 00:15:05.279
How very interesting.

00:15:06.155 --> 00:15:09.325
Very well. Since you're determined,
I'll grant the request.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:11.327
Wait! But, I won!

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:12.328
Quiet.

00:15:12.411 --> 00:15:15.664
Do you think that you're in any position
of privilege to argue?

00:15:15.748 --> 00:15:18.208
I… No, I don't…

00:15:18.792 --> 00:15:21.962
However,
let's raise the stakes for the next round.

00:15:22.546 --> 00:15:23.964
-Mikura.
-Yes.

00:15:26.216 --> 00:15:27.051
What's this?

00:15:27.134 --> 00:15:29.136
I'm laying out this collar for you.

00:15:29.219 --> 00:15:30.054
Huh?

00:15:30.137 --> 00:15:32.681
You'll become my personal house pet
if you lose.

00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:35.643
You'll come if called.

00:15:35.726 --> 00:15:37.811
You'll be sent to fetch things for me.

00:15:38.479 --> 00:15:41.523
If I tell you to keep watch,
you'll not fall asleep.

00:15:42.024 --> 00:15:42.942
And

00:15:43.984 --> 00:15:46.946
if I tell you to end your life,
you will die.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:51.742
[both gasping]

00:15:54.328 --> 00:15:56.163
[Yukimi grunting]

00:15:58.248 --> 00:16:01.168
[Mikura coughing, breathing heavily]

00:16:02.878 --> 00:16:04.797
So what'll it be, Mary?

00:16:05.673 --> 00:16:08.425
Are you certain you're ready
for that potential outcome?

00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:14.014
-Yes. I'm in.
-[Tsuzura gasping]

00:16:14.098 --> 00:16:15.182
This about this!

00:16:15.265 --> 00:16:17.059
All of this is entirely up to chance.

00:16:17.893 --> 00:16:20.938
I just lost,
so I'm sure I can win this time.

00:16:24.942 --> 00:16:26.276
[music fades]

00:16:28.988 --> 00:16:31.198
All right, then.
The game is "Three Hit Dice."

00:16:31.991 --> 00:16:34.576
This round will be the one
that decides the winner.

00:16:35.244 --> 00:16:37.329
Please write your guesses
and pass them here.

00:16:48.257 --> 00:16:50.259
[pen scribbling]

00:16:52.678 --> 00:16:55.889
<i>Mistress Juraku only wants</i>
<i>to control Saotome.</i>

00:16:56.432 --> 00:16:58.100
<i>If I want to be a good pet,</i>

00:16:58.183 --> 00:17:00.019
<i>I have to make sure she loses.</i>

00:17:00.602 --> 00:17:01.562
Here's mine.

00:17:10.195 --> 00:17:12.156
Thank you for submitting your cards.

00:17:16.368 --> 00:17:17.911
Now for the first toss.

00:17:21.331 --> 00:17:22.166
Up.

00:17:22.249 --> 00:17:23.625
Second toss.

00:17:26.253 --> 00:17:27.546
Down.

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:32.301
<i>There's a deeper level of trickiness</i>
<i>to the traps already set by this game.</i>

00:17:32.384 --> 00:17:34.219
<i>While it's true</i>
<i>that these four combinations</i>

00:17:34.303 --> 00:17:36.638
<i>have a higher probability</i>
<i>of appearing first, </i>

00:17:36.722 --> 00:17:39.975
<i>that doesn't make it any easier</i>
<i>for the gambler to win.</i>

00:17:40.059 --> 00:17:41.685
<i>Like Rock Paper Scissors,</i>

00:17:41.769 --> 00:17:44.813
<i>there's a certain compatibility</i>
<i>that makes winning possible.</i>

00:17:44.897 --> 00:17:48.150
<i>For example,</i>
<i>"U-U-D" could be your winning combination,</i>

00:17:48.233 --> 00:17:50.402
<i>but it would lose against "D-U-U."</i>

00:17:50.486 --> 00:17:51.653
<i>In this scenario,</i>

00:17:51.737 --> 00:17:55.449
<i>"D-U-U" would have a two-in-three chance</i>
<i>of winning you the match.</i>

00:17:55.532 --> 00:17:59.453
<i>This is a phenomenon where "D-U-U" has</i>
<i>a higher probability of appearing</i>

00:17:59.536 --> 00:18:01.580
<i>right before "U-U-D."</i>

00:18:01.663 --> 00:18:05.834
<i>The same truth could then be applied</i>
<i>to all resulting combinations.</i>

00:18:05.918 --> 00:18:10.089
<i>Which means</i>
<i>making sure Saotome loses is very simple.</i>

00:18:10.923 --> 00:18:13.592
<i>Being the dealer means</i>
<i>I can look at Saotome's card</i>

00:18:13.675 --> 00:18:17.971
<i>and then change Togakushi's card with one</i>
<i>that will put her at an advantage.</i>

00:18:18.055 --> 00:18:21.642
<i>In this round,</i>
<i>Saotome wrote down "U-U-U" as her guess,</i>

00:18:21.725 --> 00:18:26.855
<i>so I changed Togakushi's card to "D-U-U,"</i>
<i>which has a higher probability of winning.</i>

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:30.484
<i>Saotome's odds of winning were only 12,5%,</i>

00:18:30.567 --> 00:18:34.488
<i>but those odds all but disappeared</i>
<i>when the second toss was down.</i>

00:18:34.571 --> 00:18:35.781
Third toss.

00:18:38.283 --> 00:18:39.243
Down.

00:18:39.326 --> 00:18:43.455
<i>At this rate,</i>
<i>Saotome's loss is just a matter of time.</i>

00:18:43.539 --> 00:18:44.748
And fourth toss.

00:18:47.417 --> 00:18:48.502
Up.

00:18:48.585 --> 00:18:50.379
<i>You stupid little girl.</i>

00:18:50.462 --> 00:18:52.297
<i>You have no chance of winning.</i>

00:18:52.381 --> 00:18:54.883
<i>All you can do is pray for a win.</i>

00:18:54.967 --> 00:18:57.261
<i>What do you think of me now,</i>
<i>Mistress Juraku?</i>

00:18:58.178 --> 00:19:00.347
<i>I'm not like</i>
<i>all the other little girls in this school</i>

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.391
<i>with no brain and no follow-through.</i>

00:19:02.474 --> 00:19:05.102
<i>All I've ever wanted</i>
<i>is for you to use me--</i>

00:19:07.604 --> 00:19:08.981
[Mikura gasping]

00:19:11.233 --> 00:19:14.153
Hey! Careful! You got the cards wet!

00:19:14.236 --> 00:19:15.863
Oh. Sorry about that.

00:19:15.946 --> 00:19:18.740
<i>You're just as slow</i>
<i>and stupid as you look!</i>

00:19:18.824 --> 00:19:21.869
<i>Mistress Juraku</i>
<i>will get bored of you very quickly.</i>

00:19:23.954 --> 00:19:26.790
All right.
We'll resume the game at the fifth toss.

00:19:26.874 --> 00:19:28.709
Oh. There's no need for that.

00:19:28.792 --> 00:19:29.626
Huh?

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:32.379
I have D-D-U. That's what I wrote down.

00:19:32.462 --> 00:19:33.505
Huh?

00:19:34.131 --> 00:19:36.300
Shouldn't the dealer
have already known that?

00:19:36.383 --> 00:19:39.136
I wrote "D-D-U" on the card
before I gave it to you.

00:19:39.219 --> 00:19:41.221
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:19:41.305 --> 00:19:42.639
That wasn't what I saw.

00:19:47.352 --> 00:19:49.313
D-D-U!

00:19:49.396 --> 00:19:50.772
That means Mary wins!

00:19:50.856 --> 00:19:53.483
What did you do?

00:19:53.567 --> 00:19:55.277
How did you change what you wrote?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.529
What? Did you think
I wouldn't figure it out?

00:19:58.113 --> 00:20:00.574
This game
is basically Rock Paper Scissors.

00:20:00.657 --> 00:20:01.783
Take the first round.

00:20:01.867 --> 00:20:04.161
I noticed Togakushi's hand
was a combination

00:20:04.244 --> 00:20:06.038
that had an inherent advantage over mine.

00:20:06.121 --> 00:20:07.539
So I started to wonder.

00:20:08.498 --> 00:20:11.293
You pretty much confirmed my thoughts
in the second game.

00:20:11.376 --> 00:20:13.212
Despite the fact that she was the winner,

00:20:13.295 --> 00:20:16.131
Togakushi was still pretty hesitant
to accept it.

00:20:16.632 --> 00:20:18.133
Which leads me to believe

00:20:18.217 --> 00:20:20.302
that you swapped her card
without her knowing.

00:20:20.385 --> 00:20:24.097
Being able to change up the player's card
puts you in a pretty sweet position,

00:20:24.181 --> 00:20:25.057
wouldn't you say?

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:28.310
It's like throwing paper
after they throw rock.

00:20:28.393 --> 00:20:29.853
This doesn't make any sense.

00:20:29.937 --> 00:20:32.940
Your card had "U-U-U." I saw!

00:20:33.023 --> 00:20:34.233
You changed it! How?

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.152
I drew the vertical line in "D" with this.

00:20:37.236 --> 00:20:40.739
If you can change your answer,
then I should be able to swap mine out.

00:20:41.406 --> 00:20:42.241
What is that?

00:20:42.324 --> 00:20:44.993
Nail polish remover
with acetone is usually clear

00:20:45.077 --> 00:20:47.037
whenever you paint it
on your nails or paper.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:48.205
But if you add water,

00:20:48.288 --> 00:20:51.250
it magically becomes darker
than its surrounding colors.

00:20:51.333 --> 00:20:54.753
So, that's when it shows up
on the card as writing..

00:20:54.836 --> 00:20:57.297
Thank you so much!

00:20:57.381 --> 00:21:00.634
Because of your tells,
it was so much easier for me to win.

00:21:00.717 --> 00:21:03.470
I only had a 50-50 chance otherwise.

00:21:03.553 --> 00:21:07.766
I never would've made that second bet
without knowing you were a cheat.

00:21:09.935 --> 00:21:10.769
[Mary] Huh?

00:21:11.353 --> 00:21:12.354
Well done, ladies.

00:21:12.938 --> 00:21:16.441
No one said that you had
to use a black pen to write your guess.

00:21:16.525 --> 00:21:18.735
Even though it was done
in nail polish remover,

00:21:18.819 --> 00:21:21.363
you did write "D-D-U" on the card.

00:21:21.446 --> 00:21:23.365
If "U-U-U" had paid off,

00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:26.994
you would have kept quiet
and accepted the win, is that right?

00:21:27.077 --> 00:21:31.123
Your first bet
set your chances of losing at 87,5%

00:21:31.206 --> 00:21:33.333
With the little acetone trick you pulled,

00:21:33.417 --> 00:21:37.212
you were able to pivot that
into a 71% likelihood of winning.

00:21:37.296 --> 00:21:38.255
That deserves applause.

00:21:39.298 --> 00:21:43.260
Even with that guarantee,
you still had a 29% chance of losing.

00:21:43.343 --> 00:21:46.013
This bet
made you put your life on the line.

00:21:46.096 --> 00:21:49.141
Or did you think I was bluffing
when I proposed the results?

00:21:50.142 --> 00:21:51.143
No.

00:21:52.102 --> 00:21:54.896
Isn't that
what the core of gambling's all about?

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:57.899
I mean, I had a 71% chance of winning.

00:21:57.983 --> 00:22:00.110
I'd be stupid not to play with those odds.

00:22:00.193 --> 00:22:02.571
If you aren't willing
to take on some amount of risk,

00:22:02.654 --> 00:22:04.781
then you'll never have
the opportunity to win.

00:22:04.865 --> 00:22:07.492
If losing is the only result
when I walk away,

00:22:07.576 --> 00:22:09.911
then the only way to win is by playing.

00:22:11.788 --> 00:22:13.790
How illuminating.

00:22:14.374 --> 00:22:17.169
It's settled. Congratulations to you.

00:22:17.252 --> 00:22:19.171
This gambling den is now Mary's.

00:22:20.589 --> 00:22:22.507
You did it! Amazing!

00:22:22.591 --> 00:22:25.552
So what's gonna happen
to the literary club?

00:22:25.635 --> 00:22:26.511
Give it up.

00:22:27.095 --> 00:22:28.889
You knew you had lost the first round,

00:22:28.972 --> 00:22:31.808
but didn't argue
when Mikura declared you the winner.

00:22:31.892 --> 00:22:33.518
You played along.

00:22:34.144 --> 00:22:36.605
You have no right to protest this outcome.

00:22:37.606 --> 00:22:39.608
[somber music playing]

00:22:48.617 --> 00:22:51.036
[Mikura crying]

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:54.915
Mistress, please! I am so sorry!

00:22:54.998 --> 00:22:58.126
I failed, and I put you in this position.

00:22:58.210 --> 00:23:01.421
I need you to punish me! Mistress!

00:23:02.005 --> 00:23:03.173
You know, pet?

00:23:03.256 --> 00:23:05.842
The fact that Mary Saotome won
against her classmate

00:23:05.926 --> 00:23:07.677
on her first day is intriguing.

00:23:07.761 --> 00:23:08.595
Huh?

00:23:08.678 --> 00:23:10.430
Today was not a loss.

00:23:10.514 --> 00:23:13.642
It certainly makes me wonder
what she might really be like.

00:23:13.725 --> 00:23:15.644
But, then what about me?

00:23:15.727 --> 00:23:18.397
The setup with Togakushi
was just an excuse.

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:21.149
I didn't particularly care
about the outcome.

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:23.235
That being said,

00:23:23.318 --> 00:23:27.489
the results of this experiment
were beyond what I'd hoped for.

00:23:29.157 --> 00:23:31.827
[Sachiko] She's out of line,
brazen, and insolent,

00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:33.578
but intelligent.

00:23:34.162 --> 00:23:37.582
She believes with every part of herself
she's going to win.

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:40.335
I want to know what she sounds like

00:23:40.419 --> 00:23:43.505
when I make her cry out
like a little kitten!

00:23:46.425 --> 00:23:47.968
Mary, that was so cool!

00:23:48.051 --> 00:23:51.471
I had no idea you were gonna cinch the win
with that much style!

00:23:51.555 --> 00:23:53.098
You were such a goddess right now!

00:23:53.807 --> 00:23:55.225
Uh, that's a bit much.

00:23:55.308 --> 00:23:57.853
Getting a gambling den
was just the first part.

00:23:57.936 --> 00:24:00.981
Now I have to make money with it,
or else this whole thing is just a bust.

00:24:02.065 --> 00:24:04.860
But, you know?
It feels good to be the king.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:08.363
And now I finally have my own castle.

00:24:11.533 --> 00:24:12.993
Can I just say,

00:24:13.076 --> 00:24:15.620
I really wish I could be like you, Mary?

00:24:20.917 --> 00:24:22.377
-[Mary] Okay, fine.
-Huh?

00:24:22.461 --> 00:24:25.380
I'm trying to say
that I'll be your friend.

00:24:25.964 --> 00:24:27.466
You asked me before.

00:24:28.133 --> 00:24:29.926
But I do have one condition.

00:24:30.927 --> 00:24:33.013
Get rid of this "Mittens" tag.

00:24:33.638 --> 00:24:36.475
Don't you hate being treated
like you're some sort of animal?

00:24:36.558 --> 00:24:37.767
I wouldn't like it at all.

00:24:37.851 --> 00:24:40.770
And I'd hate my friends being treated
like that even more.

00:24:41.354 --> 00:24:42.689
But even if you didn't,

00:24:43.273 --> 00:24:44.774
I need you with me at the top.

00:24:45.484 --> 00:24:48.236
I don't want anyone
to condescend to us ever again.

00:24:48.320 --> 00:24:51.281
If gambling is the way to get respect,
then we're going to gamble.

00:24:52.199 --> 00:24:54.451
Then we'll beat all of them
at their own game.

00:25:00.874 --> 00:25:03.043
Huh? Why are you crying?

00:25:03.126 --> 00:25:04.669
Did I say something wrong?

00:25:04.753 --> 00:25:05.837
No.

00:25:06.588 --> 00:25:08.798
<i>She wants what's best for me.</i>

00:25:08.882 --> 00:25:11.176
<i>I've never had the chance</i>
<i>to think of myself as a winner.</i>

00:25:11.259 --> 00:25:13.386
<i>She's my dream girl!</i>

00:25:13.470 --> 00:25:15.180
<i>I don't know where she came from,</i>

00:25:16.056 --> 00:25:19.893
<i>but I know she rode up on a white horse</i>
<i>to give me her chivalrous hand!</i>

00:25:22.521 --> 00:25:25.315
<i>I think I found my prince!</i>

00:26:54.571 --> 00:26:55.405
[music fades]
